# Maps a mermaid block embedded in a design chapter to the pre-rendered diagram
# asset that should be used in its place.
#
#   <content-digest> <asset-stem>
#
# The digest is sha256 of the mermaid block's source, truncated to 12 hex
# characters — build.sh logs it as the cache filename when it renders a block
# locally (`[diagram] <digest>.png`). The stem is a filename stem in the
# pre-rendered diagram directory (default tools/diagrams/build/pdf/, override
# with SIMIC_DIAGRAM_DIR), without extension.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# tools/diagrams/ names its sources semantically — core-loop, observation-loop,
# assurance-loop — and those .mmd files are hand-authored decompositions, not
# copies of the mermaid block embedded in docs/design/04-architecture.md. So
# nothing matches automatically: not a content hash, not a positional index.
#
# Claiming that a hand-authored diagram faithfully replaces a chapter's own
# diagram is an editorial judgement about the design, not something this pipeline
# may infer. It is therefore recorded here, explicitly and reviewably, and left
# for the chapter owner to confirm.
#
# WITHOUT AN ENTRY the pipeline still works: it renders the chapter's own block
# locally with mmdc (PNG at 3x) and places it on a landscape page. The mapping is
# an upgrade to the shared tooling's print-themed vector output, not a dependency.
#
# PENDING OWNER DECISION
#
# 04-architecture.md §7.1 currently embeds one 20-node flowchart whose labels are
# small even on a full landscape page. tools/diagrams/core-loop.mmd is a cleaner
# rendering of the same end-to-end flow and reads considerably better. If the
# owner confirms they are equivalent for the HLD's purposes, uncomment the line
# below once `render.sh pdf` is implemented and emits core-loop into the
# pre-rendered directory:
#
# 8b061607f5ad core-loop
#
# If instead the chapter's flowchart should be split to match the three shared
# diagrams, that is a docs/design/ change and this file stays empty.
